+ * **Intel GPU buffer memory (Linux i915)**
+
+    The GPU box shows `GPU RAM (user)`: `Alloc` is the size of requested graphics buffers, and `Resident` is the portion backed by memory. These are buffer statistics for readable DRM clients owned by the current user, not total system RAM or a fixed VRAM capacity. Both system and stolen-memory regions are included.
+
+    Repeated descriptors for the same DRM client are counted once. Because fdinfo does not identify individual shared buffers across clients, shared allocations are reported as lower and upper bounds. Equal bounds appear as one value. An asterisk marks incomplete visibility (for example, a process denies access); `N/A` means no usable records were available. Other users and kernel-only allocations are outside this accounting scope. Values refresh once per second.
+
+
